  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sadashivanagar Residents Welfare ... vs State Of Karnataka on 5 November, 2025 -1- Nc: 2025:Khc:44652-Db Wp No. 13795 of 2025 Hc-Kar In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 5Th Day Of November, 2025 Present The Hon'Ble Mr. Vibhu Bakhru, Chief Justice And The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice C.M. Poonacha Writ Petition No. 13795 Of 2025 (Gm-Res) Between: 1. Sadashivanagar Residents Welfare Association Post Box No.8048, Sadashivanagar Post Office, 8Th Main, Sadashivanagar, Bengaluru 560 080.",
    "facts": "The petitioners have filed the present petition as a Public Interest Litigation, inter alia, seeking as under: i. Issue a writ of Mandamus or any other writ, order or direction to the respondent authorities to cancel the license of the establishment of a bar and restaurant (pub) named \"Eagles Perch\" at Property No. 370, 14th Cross. 8th Main, Sadashivanagar, Bangalore immediately; ii. Issue a writ of Mandamus or any other writ, order or direction to the respondent authorities not to give any No Objection Certificate/permission for starting the establishment of a bar and restaurant (pub) named \"Eagles Perch\" immediately; And iii. Issue any other writ, order or direction as this Hon'ble Court deems fit and proper under the facts & circumstances of this case in the interest of justice and equity. 2. It is the petitioners' case that the Pub/Bar named 'Eagle Perch' has been established in the premises bearing No.370, 14th Cross, 8th Main, Sadashivanagar, Bengaluru. It is contended that the site owners have obtained CL - 9 licence under the Karnataka Excise (Sale of Indian made Foreign Liquuor) Rules, 1968 and NC: 2025:KHC:44652-DB HC-KAR under Section 13 of the Karnataka Excise Act, 1965. The petitioners' objection is that the said Pub/Bar is located at a distance less than 100 metres from a religious institution, which according to the petitioners is not permissible. 3. The respondents have filed statement of objections raising several objections.",
    "arguments": "4. First, it is contended that the writ petition is not maintainable as the licencee has not been made a party to the present petition and therefore, no order against the licencee can be passed. 5. Second, it is contended that no licence has been issued to respondent No.10 [Eagles Perch]. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. First, it is contended that the writ petition is not maintainable as the licencee has not been made a party to the present petition and therefore, no order against the licencee can be passed. 5. Second, it is contended that no licence has been issued to respondent No.10 [Eagles Perch]. 6.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
